10
00:45:42,857 --> 00:45:48,857
Vicky Cristina Barcelona is a 2008 romantic comedy drama
film written and directed by Woody Allen.

11
00:50:17,142 --> 00:50:23,142
The film stars Javier Bardem, Penélope Cruz, Rebecca
Hall and Scarlett Johansson in lead roles.

12
00:54:51,428 --> 00:54:57,428
The plot centers on two American women, Vicky and Cristina, who spend a summer in Barcelona, where they meet an artist, Juan Antonio,
who is attracted to both of them, while still enamored of his mentally and emotionally unstable ex-wife María Elena.

13
00:59:25,714 --> 00:59:31,714
The film was shot in Spain in Barcelona, Avilés, and Oviedo, and was
Allen's fourth consecutive film shot outside the United States.

14
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Vicky Cristina Barcelona premiered at the 2008 Cannes Film Festival on May 17, 2008, and then received a rolling worldwide
general release that started on August 15, 2008, in the United States, and September 19, 2008, in Spain.

15
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
The film emerged as a commercial success at the box office, becoming one of Allen's
highest-grossing films by grossing $96 million against a $15 million budget.

16
01:13:08,571 --> 01:13:14,571
It received widespread critical acclaim upon release, with
particular praise directed towards Cruz's performance.

17
01:17:42,857 --> 01:17:48,857
Cruz won the Academy Award, BAFTA Award and Independent Spirit Award for Best Supporting Actress, in
addition to SAG, Golden Globe and Critics Choice nominations in the same category.

18
01:22:17,142 --> 01:22:23,142
At the 66th Golden Globe Awards, Vicky Cristina Barcelona received 4 nominations, including Best Actor in a Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy (Bardem), Best Actress
in a Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy (Hall) and Best Supporting Actress – Motion Picture (Cruz), winning Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy.

19
01:26:51,428 --> 01:26:57,428
The film explores themes of barcelona, spain,
photographer, artist, menage a trois, painter.

20
01:31:25,714 --> 01:31:31,714
The tone is emotional.
